From 89b93932c94c31863a34606bd30cc15b1a08e413 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vegetableleaf <benzhu2029@u.northwestern.edu>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:17:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] F1FIX-2: an enchanting buff on a unit whose attack
 sequence is a ramp of damage entries alone (the Inferno Dragon) runs; only
 entries that launch or act are refused

With F1FIX-1 the Rune Giant of live 010824 finds its friends, and its first enchant lands on an Inferno Dragon, which
GiantBufferBuff refused ("whose attack sequence replaces its attack"). The refusal now holds only for a sequence with
an entry that launches a projectile (Projectile / CustomFirstProjectile) or runs an action (DoAttackAction /
CustomOnAttackAction); the Inferno Dragon's three damage entries keep the row's hit hooks.
(a) for the Inferno Dragon: 010824 (FRESH1, 16.635.3, a10G1 comparator) runs exact apart from 1 torn_step frame
(2,091 exact, first div none; was 202 exact, first div 419) through 6 live enchant launches, 3 of them on an Inferno
Dragon. (b) for any other damage-only ramp (Inferno Tower cannot be enchanted: the filter leaves buildings out).
The musketeer refusal (BattleThreeMusketeersTest.anEnchantedMusketeerIsRefused) still holds.
Test: anEnchantedInfernoDragonStarts (red on both data versions with F1FIX-1 only; green after).
Core: 16.635.3 2183/0 (6 skipped); 16.402.22 2183/0 (29 skipped).
